# HabitMeasure — Cursor Rules v1.0

## PROJECT
Marketing landing page for HabitMeasure — a habit timer app.
Tagline: "Kleine gewoontes. Grote verandering. Jij meet het."
Goal: Capture waitlist emails. No working app features yet.
Audience: People (28–45) who want to build healthy habits and track progress.

## TECH STACK
- Next.js 14 (App Router)
- TypeScript (strict — no `any`)
- Tailwind CSS
- Framer Motion (animations)
- localStorage (email capture only — no backend)
- Vercel (deployment — auto-deploy on push to main)

## ROUTING
/ → Marketing landing page (only page for now)

## CODE RULES
- Read the codebase first — only change what is asked
- Add "use client" when using: useState, useEffect, onClick, Framer Motion, localStorage, window
- Use next/image for images, next/link for internal navigation
- Mobile-first. Every section must work on iPhone.
- No external images — CSS/SVG/Tailwind only for mockups
- Animations: smooth, not flashy

## BRANCH & VERSIE
- Work directly on `main` — no dev branch
- Push to main → Vercel deploys automatically (~30 sec)
- Update `package.json` version at every task
- Versie: Patch (Z) per taak · Minor (Y) per feature-groep · Major (X) bij redesign

## VERSION MANAGEMENT (required at every task)

At the end of EVERY task, always update BOTH:

1. `package.json` → Change `"version"` to the new version number
2. `lib/version.ts` → Change `APP_VERSION` to match

These must ALWAYS be in sync. Never update one without the other.

File: `lib/version.ts`
```typescript
export const APP_VERSION = 'X.Y.Z'
```

The footer reads from APP_VERSION. If you don't update lib/version.ts,
the version shown on the website will NOT change.

## COMMIT FORMAAT
vX.Y.Z type(scope): Imperatieve beschrijving (Engels, geen punt, ≤50 tekens)

Types: feat ✨ | fix 🐛 | refactor ♻️ | chore 🔧 | style 🎨 | docs 📝 | perf ⚡

Voorbeelden:
  v1.1.0 feat(mockups): Replace product preview mockups
  v1.1.1 feat(waitlist): Add Beehiiv email capture
  v1.1.2 fix(mobile): Fix overflow on small screens
  v1.0.2 chore: Add cursor rules and fix gitignore

## DESIGN SYSTEM — "Morning Energy"
Philosophy: Fresh, light, energetic, positive. Clean and minimal.
Scandinavian minimalist. White/light grey as base.
NOT dark. NOT a gym app. YES: sunny morning, fresh air.

Colors:
  bg-primary:      #FFFFFF    white — main background
  bg-surface:      #F5F7FA    light grey — cards / sections
  bg-elevated:     #ECEEF2    elevated cards
  color-teal:      #00E5C0    mint/teal — primary accent (energy, growth)
  color-teal-dark: #0C3D3A    dark teal — gradient depth
  text-primary:    #1A1A2E    dark text on light background
  text-secondary:  #6B7280    subtle text
  text-muted:      #9CA3AF    placeholder / muted
  border:          rgba(0,0,0,0.08)

Typography:
  Headlines: Plus Jakarta Sans (700, 900)
  Body:      Inter (400, 500)


Hero background:
  radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 50% at 20% 40%, rgba(168,255,62,0.06) 0%, transparent 60%),
  radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 40% at 80% 60%, rgba(255,140,66,0.05) 0%, transparent 60%),
  #0C0F14

Gradient text:
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #A8FF3E 0%, #4ECDC4 50%, #FF8C42 100%);
  -webkit-background-clip: text;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;

Primary button:
  background: #A8FF3E; color: #0C0F14; font-weight: 700;
  border-radius: 100px; padding: 14px 32px;

## FORBIDDEN
- No `pages/` directory — only `app/`
- No `any` types in TypeScript
- No hardcoded API keys or secrets
- No Supabase or backend (v1.x = marketing only)
- No external images for mockups
- Never delete code without explicit approval

## WERKWIJZE (always follow)
1. Read .cursor/rules + scan existing codebase
2. Show plan first — wait for approval
3. Execute
4. End every task with a TESTSCRIPT of max 5 points

## TESTSCRIPT (required at end of every prompt)
Format:
  ## TESTSCRIPT
  1. [Concrete action] → [Expected result]
  2. ...
  (max 5 points)

## WORKFLOW (always follow — every session)

1. Pull first
   git pull origin main

2. Snapshot (only if uncommitted work exists)
   git add .
   git commit -m "vX.Y.Z chore: Snapshot before [taskname]"
   git push origin main

3. Cursor builds (Plan Mode → review → Accept All)

4. Test locally
   npm run dev → open localhost:3000

5. Commit + push
   git add .
   git commit -m "vX.Y.Z type(scope): Description"
   git push origin main
   Write-Host "✅ vX.Y.Z live!" -ForegroundColor Green

## BRANCH RULE — CRITICAL
- ALWAYS work on `main` — never create a dev branch
- If you find yourself on a branch other than main, run:
  git checkout main
  git merge [branchname]
  git push origin main
- Do NOT create branches named: dev, feature/*, fix/*
- HabitMeasure is a solo project — no branch workflow needed
